\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}Standard number systems are $\mathbb N,\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$. Specialized notation and index ranges follow the cited source and the definitions below.


A real-valued function is computable only relative to an effective input/output representation: arbitrarily accurate outputs must be producible from appropriately represented inputs. A computable neural network similarly needs effectively given weights and activations.
\paragraph{Record scope and qualifications.}
The catalogue title is retained as metadata. Named certificates, contracts, bounds or frameworks in that title are not asserted as results of the original source extract.
The ground-truth function, sampling representation, and approximation class are not fixed. This direction overlaps source record 30004929.

Source-record limitation: The supplied assessment flags an underspecified computable-ground-truth question, also contained in retained ID 30004929.

